        "Bestiary > Magical Beasts > Turtle Family >",
        "Magma Tortoise (CR 11)",
        "XP 12,800",
        "N Huge Magical Beast (Fire, Reptilian)",
        "Init -1; Senses Darkvision 60 ft., low-light vision, scent; Perception +21"
      ],
      "DEFENSE": [
        "AC 29, touch 7, flat-footed 29 (-1 dex, +22 natural, -2 size)",
        "hp 156 [224] (14d10+84)",
        "Fort +15, Ref +8, Will +5",
        "Immune Earth; Resist Fire 10",
        "Weakness Ice"
      ],
      "OFFENSE": [
        "Speed 40 ft.",
        "Melee 2 Bites +23 (2d8+10)",
        "Space 15 ft.; Reach 15 ft.",
        "Special Abilities Magic Shell, Shell",
        "Special Attacks Breath Weapon (1d4+1 rounds, 50-ft. cone, DC 23, 8d6 fire damage)"
      ],
      "STATISTICS": [
        "Str 30, Dex 8, Con 22, Int 2, Wis 12, Cha 6",
        "Base Atk +14; CMB +24 (+26 vs. bull rush); CMD 33 (35 vs. bull rush; 37 vs. trip)",
        "Feats Awesome Blow, Awesome Charge, Cleave, Improved Bull Rush, Power Attack, Vital Strike, Weapon Focus (bite)",
        "Skills Acrobatics +18, Climb +28, Perception +21, Survival +19"
      ],
      "SPECIAL ABILITIES": [
        "Critical Attack (Ex)",
        "Once every 1d2 rounds as a standard action, the magma tortoise can inflict more pain than normal. If they succeed at hitting with their bite attack, the damage is 2d8+10 x 1.5 for total damage.",
        "Magic Shell (Su)",
        "As a move action, a fell tortoise can completely withdraw into its shell, leaving him almost completely impervious to attack. When withdrawn he cannot move or attack as long as he remains in this state, a magma tortoise gains an all Elemental Resist of 14. This cannot be active during Shell.",
        "Shell (Su)",
        "As a move action, a magma tortoise can completely withdraw into its shell, leaving him almost completely impervious to attack. When withdrawn he cannot move or attack as long as he remains in this state, a magma tortoise gains a +8 bonus to his Armor Class and a +4 bonus on Reflex saves."
      ]
    },
